process-team-loops.m's tiler spawned on the machine's GPU (docs/INPROGRESS.md,
GPU processes that run loops): its distribute loops' iterations run on the
first waves of the teams of its module's kernel that no process uses, and
the loops under parallel do in their bodies across each team's threads,
from one tile to more tiles than the GPU has teams.
REQUIRES: amdgpu-gpu

RUN: merkc -O2 -fopenmp -fdo-loops -fprocess-declarations --offload-arch=%offload-arch %libomp-flags %S/process-team-loops.m -o %t2
RUN: %gpu-env %t2 gpu | FileCheck %S/process-team-loops.m --match-full-lines --strict-whitespace

Without -fopenmp the directives are comments, and the tiler runs its loops
itself, one iteration after another.
RUN: merkc -O2 -fdo-loops -fprocess-declarations --offload-arch=%offload-arch %libomp-flags %S/process-team-loops.m -o %t.sequential
RUN: %gpu-env %t.sequential gpu | FileCheck %S/process-team-loops.m --match-full-lines --strict-whitespace

What the loops' bodies made, the arrays of the distribute loops' bodies
among them, goes with the tiler's arena when it ends.
RUN: %gpu-env MERK_CHECK_MESSAGES=1 MERK_CHECK_DEVICE_MEMORY=1 %t2 gpu 2>&1 | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=FREED
FREED: Mercury runtime: 0 messages are neither read nor freed
FREED-NEXT: Mercury runtime: 0 chunks of the devices' arenas and 0 rings are allocated
